:::info Blameless review
This review is about systems and processes, not people. Describe what happened and why each action made sense at the time.
:::

## Summary

**Severity:** :badge[SEV-2]{color=orange} · **Status:** :status[Resolved]{color=green}

:metric[—]{label="Time to detect"} :metric[—]{label="Time to mitigate"} :metric[—]{label="Users affected"}

One paragraph: what broke, who was affected, and how it ended.

## Impact

- Customer impact: failed requests, delayed data, lost revenue.
- Internal impact: teams paged, deploys frozen, support tickets.

## Timeline

All times UTC.

:::timeline
- [x] **{{today}} 00:00** — Trigger: the change or event that started it
- [x] **{{today}} 00:05** — Detection: the alert or report that surfaced it
- [x] **{{today}} 00:20** — Mitigation: what stopped the impact
- [x] **{{today}} 01:00** — Resolution: service fully recovered
:::

## Root cause

The technical cause, and the conditions that let it reach users. Keep asking "why?" until you reach something a follow-up can fix.

## Contributing factors

::::columns
:::column
**Went well**

- Detection, tooling or response that helped.
:::
:::column
**Went poorly**

- Gaps that slowed detection or recovery.
:::
::::

## Action items

- [ ] Fix that prevents recurrence :priority[P1] @owner :due[{{today}}]
- [ ] Alert or dashboard that detects this sooner :priority[P2] @owner :due[{{today}}]

:::decision{status=proposed date={{today}} owner=@owner} Process or design change agreed in the review
Why, and what it replaces.
:::

## Supporting data {agent=skip}

Graphs, logs and links to the incident channel.

:::agent Rules for follow-up work
- Link every change to its action item above and reference this postmortem in the pull request.
- Add a regression test or alert that would have caught this incident.
- Don't mark an action item done until the fix is deployed and verified.
:::
